  "recap": "The Base Invaders put together one of their most complete offensive performances of the season on Tuesday, June 30, rolling past the Stanley Slammers 20–5 behind 33 team hits and contributions up and down the lineup. Jason led the charge with a 5-for-6 night that included a home run and 4 RBI, while Mark went 4-for-5 with 3 RBI and Brendan added a 4-for-5 effort of his own with 2 RBI, giving the team three players each reaching base four or more times. Dillon chipped in a 3-for-4 game with 3 RBI, and Alex N. contributed 2 RBI on a 2-for-3 night, meaning 10 players reached base as the Invaders kept the pressure on from start to finish. With three home runs on the night and runs coming in waves, the 15-run margin was a true reflection of how cleanly everything clicked. Credit to the Slammers for competing — this one just belonged to the Invaders from early on.",
